        <name>op_type</name>
        <qualifiedname>micro_os_plus::micro_test_plus::detail::op::op_type</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Marker identifying the framework expression types. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Detected by the <computeroutput><ref refid="conceptmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1extension_1_1is__op" kindref="compound">extension::is_op</ref></computeroutput> concept, and inherited by all types derived from <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1op" kindref="compound">op</ref></computeroutput>. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
        <location file="/Users/ilg/MyProjects/micro-os-plus.github/xPacks/micro-test-plus-xpack.git/include/micro-os-plus/micro-test-plus/values.h" line="121" column="7" bodyfile="/Users/ilg/MyProjects/micro-os-plus.github/xPacks/micro-test-plus-xpack.git/include/micro-os-plus/micro-test-plus/values.h" bodystart="121" bodyend="-1"/>
      </memberdef>
    </sectiondef>
    <briefdescription>
<para>Empty base struct for the framework expression types. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1op" kindref="compound">op</ref></computeroutput> struct is the common base of the comparators defined in <computeroutput><ref refid="detail_8h" kindref="compound">detail.h</ref></computeroutput>, of <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1floating__point__constant" kindref="compound">floating_point_constant</ref></computeroutput>, and of <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1named__bool" kindref="compound">named_bool</ref></computeroutput>. It provides the <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1op_1a384b1d115e493d6a554ebda4e3089b19" kindref="member">op_type</ref></computeroutput> marker, which the <computeroutput><ref refid="conceptmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1extension_1_1is__op" kindref="compound">extension::is_op</ref></computeroutput> and <computeroutput><ref refid="conceptmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1extension_1_1any__op" kindref="compound">extension::any_op</ref></computeroutput> concepts use to distinguish the framework types from the user types, so that <computeroutput>expect()</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>require()</computeroutput>, and the operators in the <computeroutput><ref refid="namespacemicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1operators" kindref="compound">operators</ref></computeroutput> namespace accept them.</para>
<para>The types that must not have an empty base, like <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1value__base" kindref="compound">value_base</ref></computeroutput>, declare the <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1op_1a384b1d115e493d6a554ebda4e3089b19" kindref="member">op_type</ref></computeroutput> marker directly instead of deriving from <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1op" kindref="compound">op</ref></computeroutput>. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
